 "material": "preprint", "caption": "Value of the discord for Werner states \\protect{$\\frac{1-z}{4}\\Id + z\\ket{\\psi}\\bra{\\psi}$}, with \\protect{$\\ket{\\psi} =(\\ket{00}+\\ket{11})/\\sqrt{2}$}. Discord does not depend on the basis of measurement in this case because both \\protect{$\\Id$} and \\protect{$\\ket{\\psi}$} are invariant under rotations.", "label": "fig:werner", "source": "arxiv", "key": "16df6cf96a9ef52027a5a5cdcd4dbb17", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/16df6cf96a9ef52027a5a5cdcd4dbb17"}], "legacy_version": "20180602235559.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "2016-07-08", "preprint_date": "2001-05-15", "author_count": 2, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "4 pages, 2 figures, accepted for publication in Phys. Rev. Lett"}], "first_author": {"full_name": "Ollivier, Harold", "last_name": "Ollivier", "first_name": "Harold", "recid": 1953278}, "control_number": 1474471, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.88.017901"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.88.017901"}], "earliest_date": "2001-05-15", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Ollivier:2001fdq"], "abstracts": [{"source": "APS", "value": "Two classically identical expressions for the mutual information generally differ when the systems involved are quantum. This difference defines the quantum discord. It can be used as a measure of the quantumness of correlations. Separability of the density matrix describing a pair of systems does not guarantee vanishing of the discord, thus showing that absence of entanglement does not imply classicality. We relate this to the quantum superposition principle, and consider the vanishing of discord as a criterion for the preferred effectively classical states of a system, i.e., the pointer states.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "Two classically identical expressions for the mutual information generally differ when the two systems involved are quantum. We investigate this difference -- quantum discord -- and show that it can be used as a criterion for the classicality of the correlations. We also show that quantum discord can be used for describing the selection of the preferred, effectively classical, pointer states.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Introducing Quantum Discord"}], "facet_author_name": ["1953278_H. Ollivier", "981896_Wojciech H. Zurek"], "imprints": [{"date": "2001-12-14"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:1474471", "updated": "2025-10-02T07:49:27.109430"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.Lett.", "Phys. Rev. Lett."], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0105072"}]}, "created": "2016-07-08T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "1474471"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.88.017901&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}